	<!-- Export compliance: NO = Apple's "exempt" classification, NOT "no cryptography". The app does use encryption:
	     Apple's OS crypto (HTTPS) plus bundled libsodium for data confidentiality (Argon2id + XChaCha20-Poly1305
	     passphrase backups, XChaCha20-Poly1305 "Share my drive") and Ed25519 contribution signatures. All are standard,
	     published algorithms, with no proprietary crypto. Owner-confirmed App Store Connect questionnaire result, 2026-10-24:
	     "standard encryption algorithms instead of, or in addition to, Apple's OS", not distributed in France, gives
	     "you don't need to upload any documents; you can specify that you don't use encryption in Info.plist". Revisit
	     if the app adds non-standard crypto or ships in France (see ios/RELEASE.md). -->
	<key>ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption</key>
